  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Refusals change nothing",
      "items": [
        "rollback_plan refuses before any write when a path holds a later edit",
        "A missing skill directory counts as the move gap only while the journal is not applied",
        "Any status other than the four rollback-accepting ones is refused"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "What a kill leaves",
      "items": [
        "The journal keeps its last status and the kernel releases the lock",
        "Rollback after a kill: pending stays, and a missing skill directory is the journaled gap",
        "rolling-back is written before the first restore, so a retry accepts the gap",
        "rollback --apply can be retried after any number of interruptions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Explanation, not proof",
